error[E0277]: `(i32, i32)` does not start with `String`, the parameters of the parent route
  --> tests/ui/fail/route_child_params.rs:9:1
   |
 9 | / hypersig::routes! {
10 | |     fn pages(Router<()>);
11 | |     const ORG: Route<String> = "/orgs/{org}" => no_page;
12 | |     const MEMBER: Route<(i32, i32)> = "/orgs/{org}/members/{id}" in ORG => no_page;
13 | | }
   | |_^ the trait `Extends<String>` is not implemented for `(i32, i32)`
   |
   = note: a child route's parameters repeat its parent's, in order, and may add more after them
   = help: the following other types implement trait `Extends<P>`:
             `()` implements `Extends<()>`
             `(A, B)` implements `Extends<()>`
             `(A, B)` implements `Extends<(A, B)>`
             `(A, B)` implements `Extends<A>`
             `(A, B, C)` implements `Extends<()>`
             `(A, B, C)` implements `Extends<(A, B)>`
             `(A, B, C)` implements `Extends<(A, B, C)>`
             `(A, B, C)` implements `Extends<A>`
           and $N others
note: required by a bound in `hypersig::_private::child`
  --> src/lib.rs
   |
   |     pub const fn child<P: Params, Q: Search, C: Params + Extends<P>, R: Search>(
   |                                                          ^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `child`
   = note: this error originates in the macro `$crate::routes` which comes from the expansion of the macro `hypersig::routes` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)
